Hit live 2026-10-13 from CitiAI core: create(enable_ipv4 => 0, enable_ipv6 => 0) is copied verbatim into public_net -> JSON 0; the API rejects with 'failed to parse json' (invalid_input). Same for start_after_create default '// 1' (JSON 1). Callers had to pass \0/\1. Fix in the lib: coerce documented boolean params to JSON::PP::true/false (create, automount etc.). Related: GET /v1/datacenters now returns 410 deprecated_api_endpoint (Hetzner changelog 2026-06-02) — Datacenters.pm should say so / be deprecated.

Fixed: Servers->create coerces start_after_create/automount/enable_ipv4/enable_ipv6 (incl. inside public_net) and change_type upgrade_disk to JSON booleans via private _json_bool (accepts truthy/falsy, \0/\1, JSON::PP::Boolean); public_net hash copied instead of mutated. Regression t/cloud_servers_booleans.t checks encoded request content (red before, green after). Datacenters.pm POD: DEPRECATION section (live GET confirmed 410 deprecated_api_endpoint). prove -lr t/ green (58 files, 527 tests). Out of scope, noted for follow-up: Volumes->create automount passed verbatim (same bug); Volumes->attach uses $v ? \1 : \0 so a caller's \0 becomes true; CLI Cmd::Datacenter has no POD; Cloud.pm datacenters attr POD not marked deprecated (k29 is editing Cloud.pm).

